 false, "very_high_TG": false, "family_history": false, "very_high_ApoB": false, "very_high_Lp_a": false, "very_high_nonHDL": false}, "supplements": [{"dose": "1 tablet twice daily with meals", "name": "Hemagenics® Red Blood Cell Support", "caution": "Contains iron, folate, and B12 for comprehensive RBC support. Avoid taking with calcium-rich foods or dairy. May cause mild GI upset initially.", "category": "iron", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "Hemagenics provides highly absorbable iron bisglycinate with B12, B6, and folate for comprehensive red blood cell support. Indicated for functional iron deficiency, iron deficiency without anemia, and iron-responsive symptoms.", "indication": "Hemoglobin 11.9 g/dL (low)", "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "Your lab results suggest your iron stores are lower than optimal. This supplement provides a gentle, well-absorbed form of iron along with B12 and folate to support your energy levels, hair health, and overall vitality.", "supportingFindings": ["Hemoglobin 11.9 g/dL (low)"]}, {"dose": "1 tablet daily with meal", "name": "D3 2000 Complex", "caution": "Maintenance dose for suboptimal levels. Comprehensive vitamin D support with cofactors.", "category": "vitamin", "priority": "low", "rationale": "D3 2000 Complex provides maintenance vitamin D with cofactors to reach and maintain optimal range ≥60 ng/mL.", "indication": "Vitamin D 40.7 ng/mL (suboptimal, target ≥60)", "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "Your vitamin D is close to optimal but could benefit from a maintenance dose to reach the ideal range for bone and immune health.", "supportingFindings": ["Vitamin D 40.7 ng/mL (suboptimal, target ≥60)"]}, {"dose": "1 capsule daily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Women's Probiotic", "caution": "5-in-1 multi-benefit probiotic with Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 for vaginal and urinary health. Increase to 2 daily for urogenital irritation.", "category": "probiotic", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete Women's provides 5-in-1 support for vaginal, urinary, digestive, and immune health with clinically studied Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 strains.", "indication": "Foundational women's probiotic support", "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This women-specific probiotic supports digestive health, vaginal and urinary tract balance, and immune function with clinically proven strains.", "supportingFindings": ["Foundational women's probiotic support"]}], "cacStatinRec": {"statinDiscussion": {"strength": "none", "indicated": false, "rationale": ""}, "cacRecommendation": {"priority": "none", "rationale": "", "recommended": false}}, "recheckWindow": "3-6 months (routine follow-up)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall summary (plain language)\\n- Your labs show early menopause with low estrogen and a mild anemia. Key numbers: hemoglobin 11.9 g/dL (low), estradiol 15 pg/mL (low), FSH 57.7 mIU/mL (high, consistent with menopause), progesterone 0.66 ng/mL (low for HRT target), and total testosterone 14 ng/dL (low despite HRT). Other routine labs are stable: ferritin 58.2 ng/mL, TSH 0.51 mIU/L, AST 15 U/L, ALT 11 U/L, eGFR 73 mL/min.\\n\\nPositive findings\\n- Ferritin 58.2 ng/mL (stores are adequate, >50 ng/mL).\\n- Hematocrit 36%, platelets 265 K/uL (both normal).\\n- TSH 0.51 mIU/L (thyroid function in expected range).\\n- Kidney and liver tests are within expected limits (creatinine 0.97 mg/dL; AST/ALT normal).\\n- STOP-BANG 0 points = low sleep apnea risk.\\n\\nAreas to improve + concrete actions\\n1. Mild anemia: hemoglobin 11.9 g/dL\\n   - Eat iron-rich meals daily: 3–4 servings/week of lean red meat or 1 cup cooked beans/legumes, plus leafy greens (spinach) and iron-fortified cereal.\\n   - Pair iron foods with vitamin C (orange juice, bell peppers) to boost absorption; avoid tea/coffee with meals.\\n   - If you have heavy bleeding or GI symptoms, discuss further testing with your provider. Re-check hemoglobin in 8–12 weeks.\\n2. Bone health / low estrogen: estradiol 15 pg/mL (below bone-protective threshold <40 pg/mL) and FSH 57.7 mIU/mL\\n   - Weight-bearing activity 30 minutes most days and strength training 2–3x/week to protect bone.\\n   - Aim for calcium 1000–1200 mg/day from diet (dairy, fortified plant milk) and vitamin D 1000–2000 IU/day; re-check 25-OH vitamin D (currently 40.7 ng/mL) in 3 months.\\n   - Discuss a DEXA bone density scan and menopause hormone therapy options with your clinician for bone protection.\\n3. Hormone optimization: progesterone 0.66 ng/mL and total testosterone 14 ng/dL\\n   - Lifestyle: prioritize 7–8 hours sleep, strength training 2–3x/week, and stress management (walking, meditation).\\n   - Review current HRT with your provider—doses or formulation may need adjustment.\\n4. Vitamin B12 1432 pg/mL (high)\\n   - Stop or lower high-dose B12 supplements unless prescribed; review supplements with your clinician and re-check in 3 months.\\n\\nNext steps & timeline\\n- Schedule a visit in the next 2–4 weeks to review HRT and discuss DEXA if not done recently.\\n- Re-check hemoglobin, estradiol/testosterone (if HRT changed), vitamin D and B12 in 8–12 weeks after any treatment changes.\\nYou’re doing well on routine labs; these targeted steps can help with energy, bone health, and hormone balance. Please contact the clinic with any new symptoms (heavy bleeding, dark stool, chest pain, severe fatigue).", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 11.9, "status": "abnormal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "interpretation": "Low hemoglobin indicating anemia.", "recommendation": "Check iron studies, B12, folate. Evaluate menstrual blood loss if applicable.", "referenceRange": "12-16 g/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 36, "status": "normal", "category": "Hematocrit", "interpretation": "Hematocrit within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenc