ining CoQ10 production)"]}, {"dose": "2 capsules twice daily", "name": "AdvaClear®", "caution": "Broad-spectrum phase I/II liver detoxification support. Contains NAC, green tea extract, milk thistle, and B-vitamins for biotransformation. Best taken with food.", "category": "detox", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "AdvaClear provides broad-spectrum phase I and phase II liver detoxification support with NAC, green tea extract, watercress, and B-vitamins. Designed for metabolic clearance support, biotransformation of hormones and environmental compounds, and hepatic stress. Appropriate when liver markers are borderline, estrogen clearance is sluggish, or metabolic dysfunction is present.", "indication": "Insulin resistance / metabolic dysfunction (hepatic metabolic support); Borderline liver markers (ALT 19, AST 25) suggesting hepatic biotransformation load; Weight gain (metabolic clearance factor); Low energy (biotransformation burden)", "phenotypes": ["Insulin Resistance / Visceral Adiposity"], "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "This supplement supports your liver's natural detoxification processes. Your results suggest your body could benefit from help processing hormones, metabolic byproducts, and other compounds. It provides nutrients that support both phases of your liver's detox pathways.", "supportingFindings": ["Insulin resistance / metabolic dysfunction (hepatic metabolic support)", "Borderline liver markers (ALT 19, AST 25) suggesting hepatic biotransformation load", "Weight gain (metabolic clearance factor)", "Low energy (biotransformation burden)"]}, {"dose": "1 softgel 1-2 times daily", "name": "OmegaGenics® Fish Oil Neuro 1000", "caution": "High-DHA omega-3 (750mg DHA, 250mg EPA) for brain and heart health. Lemon-flavored, no fishy taste. Contains calamari - avoid if shellfish allergy.", "category": "cardiovascular", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "OmegaGenics Fish Oil Neuro 1000 provides concentrated DHA and EPA to reduce triglycerides, support brain function, cardiovascular health, and reduce systemic inflammation.", "indication": "ApoB 94 mg/dL (elevated); LDL 145 mg/dL (elevated); Total cholesterol 242 mg/dL (elevated)", "phenotypes": ["Insulin Resistance / Visceral Adiposity"], "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "This high-quality fish oil provides omega-3 fatty acids that help reduce inflammation, support your heart and brain health, and may help improve your cholesterol profile.", "supportingFindings": ["ApoB 94 mg/dL (elevated)", "LDL 145 mg/dL (elevated)", "Total cholesterol 242 mg/dL (elevated)"]}, {"dose": "2 capsules daily", "name": "GlutaClear®", "caution": "Glutathione and antioxidant support formula. Contains NAC, alpha-lipoic acid, and green tea catechins. Supports cellular defense against oxidative damage.", "category": "detox", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "GlutaClear supports glutathione production and antioxidant defense with NAC, alpha-lipoic acid, and green tea catechins. Indicated when there is evidence of oxidative stress, inflammatory burden, or metabolic dysfunction requiring enhanced cellular defense. While AdvaClear provides broader liver detoxification support, GlutaClear specifically targets glutathione pathways and antioxidant capacity.", "indication": "Insulin resistance (oxidative metabolic stress); Low energy (mitochondrial antioxidant support); Age 58 (declining glutathione production)", "phenotypes": ["Insulin Resistance / Visceral Adiposity"], "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This supplement boosts your body's master antioxidant, glutathione, which protects your cells from damage. Your results suggest increased oxidative stress, and this formula helps your body defend and repair at the cellular level.", "supportingFindings": ["Insulin resistance (oxidative metabolic stress)", "Low energy (mitochondrial antioxidant support)", "Age 58 (declining glutathione production)"]}, {"dose": "1 tablet daily with meal", "name": "D3 2000 Complex", "caution": "Maintenance dose for suboptimal levels. Comprehensive vitamin D support with cofactors.", "category": "vitamin", "priority": "low", "rationale": "D3 2000 Complex provides maintenance vitamin D with cofactors to reach and maintain optimal range ≥60 ng/mL.", "indication": "Vitamin D 52.9 ng/mL (suboptimal, target ≥60)", "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "Your vitamin D is close to optimal but could benefit from a maintenance dose to reach the ideal range for bone and immune health.", "supportingFindings": ["Vitamin D 52.9 ng/mL (suboptimal, target ≥60)"]}, {"dose": "1 capsule daily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Women's Probiotic", "caution": "5-in-1 multi-benefit probiotic with Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 for vaginal and urinary health. Increase to 2 daily for urogenital irritation.", "category": "probiotic", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete Women's provides 5-in-1 support for vaginal, urinary, digestive, and immune health with clinically studied Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 strains.", "indication": "Foundational women's probiotic support", "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This women-specific probiotic supports digestive health, vaginal and urinary tract balance, and immune function with clinically proven strains.", "supportingFindings": ["Foundational women's probiotic support"]}], "adjustedRisk": {"lpaValue": 6, "apoBValue": 94, "lpaStatus": "normal", "apoBStatus": "borderline", "riskCategory": "low", "baseASCVDRisk": 3.883700304601588, "hasElevatedLpa": false, "hasElevatedApoB": false, "adjustedCategory": "low", "clinicalGuidance": "Low risk (<5%) without risk enhancers. Focus on lifestyle modifications; reassess in 4-6 years.", "hasBorderlineLpa": false, "hasBorderlineApoB": true}, "cacStatinRec": {"statinDiscussion": {"strength": "generally_recommended", "indicated": true, "rationale": "ApoB ≥90 mg/dL (94 mg/dL) with risk enhancers (elevated ApoB). Statin discussion recommended."}, "triglycerideMgmt": {"elevated": false, "severity": "normal", "recommendation": "Triglycerides within normal range."}, "cacRecommendation": {"priority": "consider", "rationale": "Lipid levels meet threshold for CAC consideration. CAC may be useful if risk level is uncertain or patient is hesitant about statin.", "recommended": false}}, "recheckWindow": "3-6 months (routine follow-up)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall assessment\\nYour results show a menopausal hormone pattern with signs of a recent “crash” phase: FSH 67.7 mIU/mL (consistent with menopause) and estradiol 40 pg/mL (low for premenopause and somewhat higher than expected for untreated postmenopause). SHBG is high at 128 nmol/L, which lowers the amount of free sex hormones available. Cardiovascular risk is borderline: 10-year total CVD risk 6.7% and 10-year ASCVD (heart attack/stroke) risk 3.9%. Your LDL cholesterol is 145 mg/dL and ApoB is 94 mg/dL. Vitamin D is 52.9 ng/mL (adequate but suboptimal).\\n\\nPositive findings (what’s good right now)\\n- Hemoglobin 13.9 g/dL, hematocrit 41.7%, ferritin 74 ng/mL — iron stores and blood counts are healthy.\\n- TSH 0.98 mIU/L — thyroid function is normal.\\n- HDL 80 mg/dL and triglycerides 85 mg/dL — protective cholesterol pattern.\\n- eGFR 100 mL/min, AST 25 U/L, ALT 19 U/L — kidneys and liver OK.\\n- Hemoglobin A1c 5.4% — blood sugar in normal range.\\n- Lipoprotein(a) 6 mg/dL — low and favorable.\\n\\nAreas to improve + concrete actions\\n1) LDL 145 mg/dL and ApoB 94 mg/dL (borderline): \\n- Add 25–30 g fiber/day: oatmeal for breakfast, beans at lunch, vegetables at dinner.\\n- Include 2–3 servings fatty fish weekly (salmon, mackerel, sardines).\\n- Reduce saturated fat: choose lean meats, limit butter and cheese.\\n- Daily exercise: 30 minutes brisk walking (or equivalent).\\n2) Cardiovascular risk (10-year total CVD 6.7% — BORDERLINE): \\n- Aim for 150 minutes moderate aerobic activity weekly (brisk walking, cycling, swimming).\\n- Follow a Mediterranean-style diet: vegetables, whole grains, olive oil, nuts, fish; limit processed foods and added sugars.\\n- Recheck fasting lipid panel in 3 months; consider coronary artery calcium (CAC) scoring to guide statin decision — discuss with your clinician.\\n3) Hormones and bone health:\\n- FSH 67.7 mIU/mL and estradiol 40 pg/mL suggest menopause with hypoestrogenic symptoms possible. If you have hot flashes, vaginal dryness, low mood or sleep problems, discuss hormone therapy options (risks/benefits) with your provider.\\n- SHBG 128 nmol/L — please tell us if you take oral estrogen, oral contraceptives, thyroid medication, or have liver disease.\\n- Vitamin D 52.9 ng/mL: continue supplementation (typical 1,000–2,000 IU vitamin D daily) and recheck in 6–12 months. Ensure dietary calcium ~1,000–1,200 mg/day and do weight-bearing exercise; consider DEXA scan within 6–12 months given menopausal status.\\n\\nNext steps and timeline\\n- Schedule a visit to discuss menopausal symptoms, HRT options, and whether to pursue CAC or statin therapy.\\n- Lifestyle changes now (fiber, fish, exercise) and repeat fasting lipids in 3 months.\\n- Repeat vitamin D in 6–12 months; consider DEXA in 6–12 months.\\nIf you have symptoms (hot flashes, heavy bleeding, new fatigue, liver symptoms) or questions about medications that affect SHBG, contact us sooner. You’re doing well in many areas — these targeted steps can lower your cardiovascular risk and support bone and hormonal health.", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 13.9, "status": "normal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "interpretation": "Hemoglobin within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "12-16 g/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 41.7, "status": "normal", "category": "Hematocrit", "interpretation": "Hematocrit within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "36-44%"}, {"unit": "fL", "value": 95.2, "status": "normal", "category": "MCV", "interpretation": "MCV 95.2 fL is within normal range (80–100 fL), indicating normal-sized red blood cells.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "80-100 fL"}, {"unit": "K/uL", "value": 277, "status": "normal", "category": "Platelets", "interpretation": "Platelet count within normal range.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "150-400 K/uL"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 40, "status": "borderline", "category": "Estradiol", "interpretation": "Estradiol elevated for postmenopausal status without HRT.", "recommendation": "Evaluate for exogenous estrogen source or ovarian pathology. Consider HRT if symptomatic.", "referenceRange": "<20 pg/mL (postmenopausal without HRT)"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 0.39, "status": "normal", "category": "Progesterone", "interpretation": "Progesterone appropriate for postmenopausal status.", "recommendation": "Expected finding.", "referenceRange": "<1 ng/mL (postmenopausal)"}, {"unit": "mIU/mL", "value": 67.7, "status": "normal", "category": "FSH", "interpretation": "Elevated FSH consistent with menopause.", "recommendation": "Expected finding for postmenopausal women.", "referenceRange": ">25 mIU/mL (postmenopausal)"}, {"unit": "ng/dL", "value": 28.7, "status": "normal", "category": "Testosterone (Total)", "interpretation": "Testosterone within normal female range.", "recommendation": "No intervention needed.", "referenceRange": "15-70 ng/dL"}, {"unit": "mIU/L", "value": 0.98, "status": "normal", "category": "TSH", "interpretation": "TSH within normal range - euthyroid.", "recommendation": "No thyroid intervention needed.", "referenceRange": "0.4-4.5 mIU/L"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 74, "status": "normal", "category": "Ferritin", "interpretation": "Ferritin within optimal range (>50).", "recommendation": "Adequate iron stores. No supplementation need