ge)"]}, {"name": "Oxidative Stress Burden", "confidence": "high", "description": "Multiple markers suggest increased oxidative stress and cellular burden. Antioxidant and glutathione support may help reduce oxidative damage and support cellular energy production.", "supportingFindings": ["hs-CRP 3.3 mg/L (elevated, systemic inflammation)", "AST 24 U/L (cellular stress marker)", "Insulin resistance pattern (metabolic oxidative driver)", "A1c 5.7% (glycemic stress)", "Triglycerides 363 mg/dL (lipid peroxidation risk)", "Low energy / fatigue (possible mitochondrial burden)", "Age 70 (increased oxidative stress risk)"]}, {"name": "Estrogen Dominance / Impaired Clearance", "confidence": "moderate", "description": "Lab pattern consistent with relative estrogen excess or impaired estrogen clearance. Even without reported symptoms, supporting liver detoxification and estrogen metabolism pathways may be beneficial.", "supportingFindings": ["Elevated estradiol 170 pg/mL", "Borderline liver markers (ALT 18, AST 24) suggesting possible impaired hepatic clearance"]}, {"name": "Iron Deficiency", "confidence": "low", "description": "Iron stores are depleted or suboptimal. Iron is essential for energy, cognitive function, hair health, and oxygen transport.", "supportingFindings": ["Ferritin 42.8 ng/mL (suboptimal ≤50)", "Low energy/fatigue reported"]}]}	\N	2026-04-02 16:34:09.53801	2026-04-02 16:34:09.53801
