ted; Headaches reported (hormone-related)", "phenotypes": ["Estrogen Dominance / Impaired Clearance"], "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "This supplement helps your body process and balance estrogen more effectively. It supports healthy hormone metabolism, which can help with PMS symptoms, bloating, mood changes, and hormonal balance during life transitions.", "supportingFindings": ["Estrogen dominance / impaired clearance phenotype detected", "Headaches reported (hormone-related)"]}, {"dose": "2 capsules twice daily", "name": "AdvaClear®", "caution": "Broad-spectrum phase I/II liver detoxification support. Contains NAC, green tea extract, milk thistle, and B-vitamins for biotransformation. Best taken with food.", "category": "detox", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "AdvaClear provides broad-spectrum phase I and phase II liver detoxification support with NAC, green tea extract, watercress, and B-vitamins. Designed for metabolic clearance support, biotransformation of hormones and environmental compounds, and hepatic stress. Appropriate when liver markers are borderline, estrogen clearance is sluggish, or metabolic dysfunction is present.", "indication": "Estrogen dominance pattern (hepatic detox pathways needed for clearance); Low energy (biotransformation burden)", "phenotypes": ["Estrogen Dominance / Impaired Clearance"], "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This supplement supports your liver's natural detoxification processes. Your results suggest your body could benefit from help processing hormones, metabolic byproducts, and other compounds. It provides nutrients that support both phases of your liver's detox pathways.", "supportingFindings": ["Estrogen dominance pattern (hepatic detox pathways needed for clearance)", "Low energy (biotransformation burden)"]}, {"dose": "1 soft chew during times of stress", "name": "HerWellness™ Rapid Stress Relief", "caution": "Fast-acting L-Theanine and Lactium formula. Non-drowsy. Promotes calm within 1 hour. Contains milk.", "category": "hormone-support", "priority": "low", "rationale": "HerWellness Rapid Stress Relief provides fast-acting stress support with L-Theanine (200mg) and Lactium. Promotes calm within 1 hour without drowsiness.", "indication": "Anxiety reported", "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This fast-acting supplement helps your body respond to stress more calmly. It promotes relaxation within about an hour and can be taken as needed without causing drowsiness.", "supportingFindings": ["Anxiety reported"]}, {"dose": "1 capsule daily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Women's Probiotic", "caution": "5-in-1 multi-benefit probiotic with Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 for vaginal and urinary health. Increase to 2 daily for urogenital irritation.", "category": "probiotic", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete Women's provides 5-in-1 support for vaginal, urinary, digestive, and immune health with clinically studied Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 strains.", "indication": "Foundational women's probiotic support", "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This women-specific probiotic supports digestive health, vaginal and urinary tract balance, and immune function with clinically proven strains.", "supportingFindings": ["Foundational women's probiotic support"]}], "cacStatinRec": {"statinDiscussion": {"strength": "none", "indicated": false, "rationale": ""}, "cacRecommendation": {"priority": "none", "rationale": "CAC generally less informative under age 40. Consider if extreme family history with very high Lp(a).", "recommended": false}}, "recheckWindow": "2-4 weeks (urgent values present)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall assessment (plain language)\\nYour labs show a pattern called “estrogen dominance” with an elevated estradiol of 181 pg/mL and a low progesterone of 0.6 ng/mL. This usually reflects ovulatory dysfunction in perimenopause rather than too much estrogen production. You also have severely low iron stores (ferritin 8.8 ng/mL) even though your hemoglobin is still normal (12 g/dL). Vitamin D is a bit low at 31.3 ng/mL. Your total testosterone is 22.1 ng/dL (reported as low despite HRT); free testosterone is 3 pg/mL and SHBG is 43.8 nmol/L.\\n\\nPositive findings\\n- Hemoglobin 12 g/dL and hematocrit 37.2% are within the normal range.\\n- MCV 89.2 fL, platelets 279 K/uL, and FSH 11.9 mIU/mL are within expected ranges.\\n- STOP-BANG score 0 = low risk for sleep apnea.\\n\\nAreas to improve (with specific actions)\\n1) Estradiol 181 pg/mL / Progesterone 0.6 ng/mL — estrogen dominance:\\n   - Urgent: physician review required before any hormone changes.\\n   - Lifestyle: prioritize sleep hygiene (7–8 hours nightly), reduce excess alcohol, avoid caffeine late afternoon (may lower nighttime anxiety/3am waking), and track bleeding patterns and symptoms (breast tenderness, migraines, heavy/irregular cycles).\\n   - If you have heavy or irregular bleeding, ask your clinician about progesterone (cyclic) to protect the uterine lining.\\n\\n2) Ferritin 8.8 ng/mL (severely low):\\n   - Start oral iron: aim for ~60–65 mg elemental iron (for example ferrous sulfate 325 mg = 65 mg elemental) every other day with 250–500 mg vitamin C or a glass of orange juice to improve absorption. Take away from calcium, coffee/tea. Continue for at least 8–12 weeks and recheck ferritin and CBC.\\n   - Eat iron-rich foods daily: lean red meat, lentils/beans, spinach, iron-fortified cereal; cook in cast-iron pans.\\n\\n3) Vitamin D 31.3 ng/mL (insufficient):\\n   - Start vitamin D3 1,000–2,000 IU daily and recheck 25-OH vitamin D in 8–12 weeks.\\n\\n4) Testosterone 22.1 ng/dL (low):\\n   - Lifestyle to support testosterone: 7–8 hours quality sleep, strength training 2–3x weekly, manage stress with exercise, meditation or hobbies, and maintain healthy body weight.\\n\\nNext steps and timeline\\n- Physician review is needed urgently for the hormone pattern (estradiol/progesterone) before changing HRT.\\n- Begin iron therapy now and recheck ferritin + CBC in 8–12 weeks.\\n- Start vitamin D3 and recheck in 8–12 weeks.\\n- Consider a follow-up hormone panel after any HRT adjustment in ~6–12 weeks and continue tracking symptoms and bleeding; reach out sooner if you develop heavy bleeding, severe headaches, or new symptoms.\\n\\nIf you’d like, we can schedule a follow-up visit to review these results and make a specific treatment plan.", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 12, "status": "normal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "interpretation": "Hemoglobin within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "12-16 g/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 37.2, "status": "normal", "category": "Hematocrit", "interpretation": "Hematocrit within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "36-44%"}, {"unit": "fL", "value": 89.2, "status": "normal", "category": "MCV", "interpretation": "MCV 89.2 fL is within normal range (80–100 fL), indicating normal-sized red blood cells.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "80-100 fL"}, {"unit": "K/uL", "value": 279, "status": "normal", "category": "Platelets", "interpretation": "Platelet count within normal range.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "150-400 K/uL"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 181, "status": "abnormal", "category": "Estradiol", "interpretation": "Estradiol elevated above typical HRT range.", "recommendation": "Provider recommendation: Evaluate estrogen dose. Monitor for estrogen excess symptoms.", "referenceRange": "60-100 pg/mL (HRT goal, >40 for bone)"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 0.6, "status": "abnormal", "category": "Progesterone", "interpretation": "Progesterone below HRT therapeutic range.", "recommendation": "Provider recommendation: Increase progesterone dose. Target 8-10 ng/mL for optimal endometrial protection.", "referenceRange": "8-10 ng/mL (HRT goal)"}, {"unit": "mIU/mL", "value": 11.9, "status": "normal", "category": "FSH", "interpretation": "FSH level recorded.", "recommendation": "For accurate interpretation, document cycle phase.", "referenceRange": "3-20 mIU/mL (varies by phase)"}, {"unit": "ng/dL", "value": 22.1, "status": "abnormal", "category": "Testosterone (Total)", "interpretation": "Low testosterone despite HRT.", "recommendation": "Provider recommendation: Increase testosterone dose. Target 75-125 ng/dL for optimal results.", "referenceRange": "75-125 ng/dL (HRT goal)"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 8.8, "status": "critical", "category": "Ferritin", "interpretation": "Severely depleted iron stores without anemia.", "recommendation": "Provider protocol: Metagenics Hemagenics OR Prescription 65mg Elemental Iron (take every other day, on empty stomach, avoid caffeine and dairy 2 hours before/after). Evaluate for blood loss.", "referenceRange": ">50 ng/mL (optimal)"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 31.3, "status": "borderline", "category": "Vitamin D (25-OH)", "interpretation": "Vitamin D insufficient (31-40 ng/mL). Suboptimal for hormone optimization.", "recommendation": "Metagenics D3 5,000 + K daily. Target ≥60 ng/mL.", "referenceRange": "≥60 ng/mL optimal"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 181, "status": "abnormal", "category": "Perimenopause Assessment: Estrogen Dominance Pattern", "interpretation": "Estradiol of 181 pg/mL with progesterone of only 0.6 ng/mL represents estrogen dominance. This is not excess estrogen production — it reflects ovulatory dysfunction where estrogen continues but ovulation (and thus progesterone) fails. Associated symptoms include insomnia or 3am waking, anxiety, breast tenderness, migraines, and heavy or irregular cycles.", "recommendation": "PROVIDER RECOMMENDATION: Add progesterone first — do not attempt to suppress estrogen. Micronized progesterone 100–200 mg nightly provides opposition and symptom relief. Avoid language about \\"too much estrogen\\" — the issue is inadequate progesterone from anovulatory cycles. PATIENT EDUCATION: Your estrogen is in the higher range, but the real issue is that progesterone hasn't kept up. This happens when ovulation becomes irregular in perimenopause. Adding progesterone will help balance things out and relieve symptoms like heavy periods, breast tenderness, and mood swings.", "referenceRange": "E2 >150 with P4 <5 indicates unopposed estrogen"}, {"unit": "nmol/L", "value": 43.8, "status": "normal", "category": "SHBG", "interpretation": "SHBG 43.8 nmol/L is within normal range. SHBG regulates bioavailable sex hormones by binding testosterone and estradiol.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "24-122 nmol/L"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 3, "status": "normal", "category": "Free Testosterone", "interpretation": "Free testosterone 3 pg/mL is within normal functional range.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "0.5-5.0 pg/mL"}, {"unit": "points", "value": 0, "status": "normal", "category": "Sleep Apnea Risk (STOP-BANG)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "LOW RISK for obstructive sleep apnea (0/8 points)", "recommendation": "Low probability of moderate-severe OSA. Continue routine monitoring. Consider sleep study if persistent symptoms of excessive daytime sleepiness, loud snoring, or cardiovascular risk factors.", "referenceRange": "Low 0-2, Intermediate 3-4, High 5-8"}], "aiRecommendations": "Unable to generate recommendations. Please review lab findings manually.", "clinicalPhenotypes": [{"name": "Iron Deficiency", "confidence": "high", "description": "Iron stores are depleted or suboptimal. Iron is essential for energy, cognitive function, hair health, and oxygen transport.", "supportingFindings": ["Ferritin 8.8 ng/mL (severely depleted ≤20)", "Low energy/fatigue reported"]}, {"name": "Estrogen Dominance / Impaired Clearance", "confidence": "moderate", "description": "Lab pattern consistent with relative estrogen excess or impaired estrogen clearance. Even without reported symptoms, supporting liver detoxification and estrogen metabolism pathways may be beneficial.", "supportingFindings": ["Estradiol:Progesterone imbalance (E2 181, P4 0.6)", "Progesterone 0.6 ng/mL (very low)", "Headaches reported"]}]}	2026-03-26 19:28:27.375013	1
