endation": "Lifestyle modifications recommended. Statin generally not indicated at current risk level.", "tenYearCVDPercentage": "2.8%", "tenYearASCVDPercentage": "1.9%", "thirtyYearHFPercentage": "7.5%", "thirtyYearHeartFailure": 0.07468382205319349, "thirtyYearCVDPercentage": "18.5%", "thirtyYearASCVDPercentage": "11.8%"}, "supplements": [{"dose": "1 softgel 1-2 times daily", "name": "OmegaGenics® Fish Oil Neuro 1000", "caution": "High-DHA omega-3 (750mg DHA, 250mg EPA) for brain and heart health. Lemon-flavored, no fishy taste. Contains calamari - avoid if shellfish allergy.", "category": "cardiovascular", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "OmegaGenics Fish Oil Neuro 1000 provides concentrated DHA and EPA to reduce triglycerides, support brain function, cardiovascular health, and reduce inflammation.", "indication": "TG 236 mg/dL, HDL 29 mg/dL (low)"}, {"dose": "1 chewable gel daily", "name": "NutraGems® CoQ10 300", "caution": "Chewable 300mg CoQ10 in emulsified form for enhanced absorption. Supports heart muscle function, energy production, and antioxidant protection. Essential for patients on statins.", "category": "cardiovascular", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "NutraGems CoQ10 300 provides high-potency ubiquinone for cardiovascular protection, cellular energy production, and antioxidant support. Essential for patients on statins.", "indication": "HDL 29 mg/dL (low), TG 236 mg/dL"}, {"dose": "1 capsule daily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Probiotic", "caution": "Multi-strain probiotic for digestive and immune health. Shelf-stable formula. No refrigeration needed.", "category": "general", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete provides comprehensive multi-strain probiotic support for digestive health, immune function, and overall wellness.", "indication": "Men's health foundation"}, {"dose": "1 tablet daily with meal", "name": "D3 2000 Complex", "caution": "Maintenance dose for suboptimal levels. Comprehensive vitamin D support with cofactors.", "category": "vitamin", "priority": "low", "rationale": "D3 2000 Complex provides maintenance vitamin D with cofactors to reach optimal range ≥60 ng/mL for testosterone and immune support.", "indication": "Vitamin D 57.9 ng/mL (suboptimal, target ≥60)"}], "recheckWindow": "8-12 weeks (after dose change or intervention)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall assessment (plain language)\\n- Many values are in a safe range, but a few results need attention: your HDL is low at 29 mg/dL, triglycerides are high at 236 mg/dL, free testosterone is high at 279 pg/mL with low SHBG at 18.6 nmol/L, STOP-BANG sleep-apnea score is 4 (intermediate risk), and creatinine is borderline at 1.43 mg/dL. Your 10‑year CVD risk is low (10‑year ASCVD 1.9%, 10‑year total CVD 2.8%), but your 30‑year CVD risk is 18.5% (meaning over 30 years you have about an 18.5% chance of a major CVD event), which falls into the INTERMEDIATE risk range — so stronger prevention steps are appropriate.\\n\\nPositive findings\\n- Hemoglobin 14.3 g/dL and hematocrit 47.3% (safe for continued TRT).\\n- LDL 84 mg/dL (within optimal range).\\n- eGFR 61 mL/min and BUN 12 mg/dL (kidney function currently acceptable).\\n- PSA 1.69 ng/mL, TSH 1.23 mIU/L, Vitamin B12 571 pg/mL, Vitamin D 25‑OH 57.9 ng/mL (adequate/suboptimal).\\n\\nAreas to improve (specific values + concrete actions)\\n- HDL cholesterol 29 mg/dL (low) and triglycerides 236 mg/dL (high). Actions:\\n  - Add 25–30 g fiber daily: oatmeal for breakfast, beans with lunch, vegetables at dinner.\\n  - Include 2–3 servings fatty fish weekly (salmon, mackerel, sardines).\\n  - Reduce saturated fat: choose lean meats, limit butter and cheese.\\n  - Daily exercise: 30 minutes brisk walking or equivalent.\\n- Cardiovascular prevention (30‑year CVD risk 18.5% = INTERMEDIATE): follow stronger prevention steps:\\n  - Increase to 200–300 minutes aerobic exercise weekly plus strength training 2×/week.\\n  - Focus on heart‑healthy fats: avocados, nuts, olive oil, fatty fish 3× weekly.\\n  - Reduce sodium to <2,300 mg/day: avoid processed foods, choose fresh ingredients.\\n  - If you smoke: strongly consider quitting. Discuss statin therapy with your provider if lifestyle changes don’t lower risk.\\n- Free testosterone 279 pg/mL (elevated) and SHBG 18.6 nmol/L (low), total testosterone 873 ng/dL (upper end). This pattern suggests supraphysiologic dosing of testosterone. Actions:\\n  - Do not change medication without consulting your prescriber. Schedule a visit within 1–2 weeks to review dosing and administration.\\n  - Consider pausing extra/dose increases until discussed. Repeat testosterone panel 4–6 weeks after any dosing change.\\n- STOP‑BANG 4/8 = INTERMEDIATE sleep apnea risk. Actions:\\n  - Avoid alcohol/sedatives within 3 hours of bedtime, maintain regular sleep schedule, and schedule a sleep medicine referral for a sleep study.\\n- Creatinine 1.43 mg/dL (borderline): hydrate well, avoid regular NSAIDs, recheck BMP in 4 weeks; if persistent, consider nephrology referral.\\n\\nNext steps and timeline\\n- Schedule clinic visit in 1–2 weeks to review testosterone regimen and sleep‑apnea referral.\\n- Recheck fasting lipids and metabolic panel in ~8–12 weeks after lifestyle changes.\\n- Repeat testosterone/free T and SHBG 4–6 weeks after any medication change.\\n- Follow up on sleep study referral as recommended.\\n\\nYou’re doing many things right — these targeted steps can lower your long‑term risk. If you want, I can help make a 12‑week plan (meals, workouts, supplements) and draft questions for your provider visit.", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 14.3, "status": "normal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "recheckTiming": "", "interpretation": "Hemoglobin within normal range for adult males.", "recommendation": "Continue current testosterone regimen.", "referenceRange": "13.5-17.5 g/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 47.3, "status": "normal", "category": "Hematocrit", "recheckTiming": "Per standard monitoring schedule", "interpretation": "Hematocrit <50%. Within safe range for TRT continuation.", "recommendation": "Continue TRT with routine monitoring per protocol.", "referenceRange": "<50% (target), 50-52% (caution), 52-54% (high risk), ≥54% (critical)"}, {"unit": "fL", "value": 90.1, "status": "normal", "category": "MCV", "interpretation": "MCV 90.1 fL is within normal range (80–100 fL), indicating normal-sized red blood cells.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "80-100 fL"}, {"unit": "ng/dL", "value": 873, "status": "borderline", "category": "Testosterone (Total)", "recheckTiming": "8-12 weeks", "interpretation": "Testosterone at upper end of target range - consider symptoms.", "recommendation": "Provider recommendation: If asymptomatic, maintain dose. If symptomatic (anxiety, irritability, acne), reduce 10%.", "referenceRange": "400-700 ng/dL (trough target)"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 23, "status": "normal", "category": "Estradiol", "interpretation": "Estradiol within expected range for men on TRT.", "recommendation": "No intervention needed. Estradiol is beneficial for bone and cardiovascular health.", "referenceRange": "20-60 pg/mL"}, {"unit": "U/L", "value": 26, "status": "normal", "category": "AST", "recheckTiming": "", "interpretation": "AST within normal limits.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "<40 U/L"}, {"unit": "U/L", "value": 38, "status": "normal", "category": "ALT", "recheckTiming": "", "interpretation": "ALT within normal limits.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "<40 U/L"}, {"unit": "mL/min", "value": 61, "status": "normal", "category": "eGFR", "recheckTiming": "", "interpretation": "Normal kidney function (eGFR ≥60).", "recommendation": "Routine care and monitoring.", "referenceRange": "≥60 mL/min"}, {"unit": "mg/dL", "value": 1.43, "status": "borderline", "category": "Creatinine", "recheckTiming": "2-4 weeks", "interpretation": "Borderline creatinine elevation.", "recommendation": "Encourage hydration. Recheck in 2-4 weeks.", "referenceRange": "≤1.3 mg/dL"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 1.69, "status": "normal", "category": "PSA", "interpretation": "PSA within normal limits.", "recommendation": "Continue monitoring per protocol (baseline, 3-12 mo, then per risk).", "referenceRange": "<4.0 ng/mL"}, {"unit": "mg/dL", "value": 84, "status": "normal", "category": "LDL Cholesterol", "interpretation": "LDL within optimal range.", "recommendation": "Maintain heart-healthy lifestyle. Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "<130 mg/dL (optimal)"}, {"unit": "mg/dL", "value": 236, "status": "borderline", "category": "Triglycerides", "interpretation": "Triglycerides elevated. Lifestyle and metabolic optimization needed.", "recommendation": "Reduce refined carbs, minimize alcohol. Increase physical activity. Omega-3 supplementation. Repeat in 3 months.", "referenceRange": "<150 mg/dL (optimal)"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 2.8320223573465637, "status": "normal", "category": "10-Year Total CVD Risk (PREVENT)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "10-year cardiovascular disease risk: 2.8% (LOW RISK). Includes ASCVD and heart failure.", "recommendation": "Heart-healthy lifestyle: Mediterranean diet, regular exercise (150 min/week), maintain healthy weight, smoking cessation\\n\\nLOW RISK (<5%): Focus on lifestyle modifications\\n\\nReassess risk in 4-6 years", "referenceRange": "Low <5%, Borderline 5-7.4%, Intermediate 7.5-19.9%, High ≥20%"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 1.8931963273923615, "status": "normal", "category": "10-Year ASCVD Risk (PREVENT)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "10-year ASCVD risk (heart attack, stroke): 1.9%", "recommendation": "Lifestyle modifications recommended. Statin generally not indicated at current risk level.", "referenceRange": "Heart attack & stroke risk"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 0.8186389111476065, "s