": "L-Threonate form crosses blood-brain barrier for cognitive and sleep support. Well-tolerated; gentle on GI system.", "category": "mineral", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "Magtein is the only magnesium form shown to effectively cross the blood-brain barrier. Supports quality sleep, cognitive function, and hormonal balance.", "indication": "Multiple metabolic/hormonal stress indicators"}, {"dose": "2 capsules twice daily", "name": "Adreset®", "caution": "Adaptogenic formula with ginseng, rhodiola, and cordyceps. Best taken earlier in day. May take 2-4 weeks for full effect.", "category": "hormone-support", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "Adreset combines adaptogenic herbs to support healthy adrenal function, stress resilience, and energy. Helps restore HPA axis balance and supports testosterone production.", "indication": "Total T 337 ng/dL (low)"}, {"dose": "2 tablets daily", "name": "Exhilarin®", "caution": "Ayurvedic adaptogenic formula. Supports mental clarity and emotional well-being. Takes 2-4 weeks for optimal benefits.", "category": "general", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "Exhilarin provides adaptogenic support for mental energy, mood, and stress resilience. Complements hormonal optimization for comprehensive fatigue management.", "indication": "Multiple fatigue factors: Total T 337, A1c 6%, Glucose 115"}, {"dose": "1 softgel 1-2 times daily", "name": "OmegaGenics® Fish Oil Neuro 1000", "caution": "High-DHA omega-3 (750mg DHA, 250mg EPA) for brain and heart health. Lemon-flavored, no fishy taste. Contains calamari - avoid if shellfish allergy.", "category": "cardiovascular", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "OmegaGenics Fish Oil Neuro 1000 provides concentrated DHA and EPA to reduce triglycerides, support brain function, cardiovascular health, and reduce inflammation.", "indication": "TG 253 mg/dL, HDL 32 mg/dL (low)"}, {"dose": "1 capsule daily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Probiotic", "caution": "Multi-strain probiotic for digestive and immune health. Shelf-stable formula. No refrigeration needed.", "category": "general", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete provides comprehensive multi-strain probiotic support for digestive health, immune function, and overall wellness.", "indication": "Men's health foundation"}, {"dose": "1 tablet daily with meal", "name": "D3 2000 Complex", "caution": "Maintenance dose for suboptimal levels. Comprehensive vitamin D support with cofactors.", "category": "vitamin", "priority": "low", "rationale": "D3 2000 Complex provides maintenance vitamin D with cofactors to reach optimal range ≥60 ng/mL for testosterone and immune support.", "indication": "Vitamin D 55.9 ng/mL (suboptimal, target ≥60)"}], "recheckWindow": "8-12 weeks (after dose change or intervention)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall assessment (plain language)\\n- Your labs show some strengths but also several areas that need attention. Key concerns: hemoglobin 13.2 g/dL (low), STOP-BANG 5/8 (high risk for sleep apnea), HDL 32 mg/dL (low), triglycerides 253 mg/dL (high), A1c 6.0% and fasting glucose 115 mg/dL (both in the prediabetes range), and total testosterone 337 ng/dL (below optimal). Your 10-year ASCVD risk is low at 2.3%, but your 30-year CVD risk is 23.4% (elevated long-term risk), so stronger prevention steps are recommended.\\n\\nPositive findings\\n- Hematocrit 44%, MCV 86.8 fL, RBC 5.07 M/µL, WBC 7.3 K/µL, platelets 239 K/µL are all in normal ranges.\\n- LDL 86 mg/dL is within an optimal range.\\n- AST 28 U/L, FIB-4 score 0.83 (low fibrosis risk), eGFR 64 mL/min, BUN 16 mg/dL, bilirubin 0.4 mg/dL are reassuring.\\n- Vitamin B12 690 pg/mL and Vitamin D 55.9 ng/mL are adequate.\\n\\nAreas to improve (values + concrete actions)\\n- Hemoglobin 13.2 g/dL (low): Get iron studies (ferritin, iron, TIBC). Meanwhile eat iron-rich foods (red meat, spinach, beans) and include vitamin C with meals to boost absorption. Follow up in 6–8 weeks.\\n- Sleep Apnea STOP-BANG 5/8 (HIGH RISK): Arrange a sleep study (home or lab) as soon as possible. Losing weight and avoiding alcohol at bedtime can help; position therapy and CPAP may be recommended after testing.\\n- HDL 32 mg/dL and triglycerides 253 mg/dL: Add 25–30 g fiber daily (oatmeal breakfast, beans at lunch, vegetables at dinner). Include 2–3 servings fatty fish weekly (salmon, mackerel, sardines). Reduce saturated fat (choose lean meats, limit butter/cheese). Daily exercise: 30 minutes brisk walking or equivalent.\\n- A1c 6.0% and fasting glucose 115 mg/dL (prediabetes): Reduce refined carbs (swap white bread for whole grain, limit sugary drinks). Include protein with each meal. Walk 10–15 minutes after meals. Recheck A1c in 3 months.\\n- Total testosterone 337 ng/dL (goal 600–1200): Prioritize 7–8 hours quality sleep, strength train 2–3× weekly, and manage stress with exercise or meditation. Discuss repeat morning testosterone and further evaluation with your provider.\\n- ALT 42 U/L and creatinine 1.38 mg/dL (borderline): Limit alcohol to <2 drinks/week, review supplements/medications that stress the liver, maintain healthy weight. Stay well hydrated and avoid NSAID overuse. Repeat labs in 6–8 weeks.\\n\\nNext steps and timeline\\n- Schedule: sleep study ASAP; iron studies + repeat CBC in 6–8 weeks; repeat fasting glucose/A1c in 3 months; repeat lipids and ALT in 3 months after lifestyle changes.\\n- Discuss these results with your provider to decide on additional testing or treatments (including discussion of long-term CVD risk and whether medications like statins are appropriate).\\nYou’re already doing some things well—these targeted steps can meaningfully lower your risks. If you want, we can make a specific 8–12 week plan together.", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 13.2, "status": "abnormal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "recheckTiming": "4-6 weeks", "interpretation": "Low hemoglobin may indicate anemia.", "r