n help manage symptoms like hot flashes, sleep problems, and vaginal dryness while also protecting bone health.", "referenceRange": "FSH <25 mIU/mL premenopausal; ≥25 suggests transition; ≥40 menopausal"}], "aiRecommendations": "Unable to generate recommendations. Please review lab findings manually.", "insulinResistance": {"markers": [{"name": "TG:HDL Ratio", "value": 5.66, "detail": "Triglycerides 249 / HDL 44 = 5.66", "positive": true, "threshold": ">= 3.0"}, {"name": "A1c", "value": "5%", "detail": "Normal glycemic control", "positive": false, "threshold": ">= 5.7%"}, {"name": "ALT", "value": 22, "detail": "Within optimal range", "positive": false, "threshold": "> 25 U/L (optimal)"}], "likelihood": "none", "phenotypes": [], "positiveCount": 1, "likelihoodLabel": "LOW LIKELIHOOD", "providerSummary": "INSULIN RESISTANCE SCREENING: LOW LIKELIHOOD (1/6 markers positive). No significant insulin resistance pattern detected at this time.", "confirmationTests": ""}, "clinicalPhenotypes": [{"name": "Menopausal Transition", "confidence": "high", "description": "Clinical picture consistent with perimenopause or menopause. Hormonal shifts during this transition affect bone health, cardiovascular risk, mood, and quality of life.", "supportingFindings": ["Age 54 (perimenopause window)", "FSH 70.9 mIU/mL (elevated, menopausal range)", "Estradiol 5 pg/mL (declining)"]}, {"name": "Estrogen Dominance / Impaired Clearance", "confidence": "moderate", "description": "Lab pattern consistent with relative estrogen excess or impaired estrogen clearance. Even without reported symptoms, supporting liver detoxification and estrogen metabolism pathways may be beneficial.", "supportingFindings": ["Progesterone 0.19 ng/mL (very low)", "Borderline liver markers (ALT 22, AST 31) suggesting possible impaired hepatic clearance"]}, {"name": "Oxidative Stress Burden", "confidence": "moderate", "description": "Multiple markers suggest increased oxidative stress and cellular burden. Antioxidant and 