117 mg/dL (atherogenic metabolic pattern); hs-CRP 3.3 mg/L (metabolic inflammation)", "phenotypes": ["Insulin Resistance / Visceral Adiposity", "Inflammatory Burden"], "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "This specialized probiotic contains Akkermansia, a beneficial gut bacteria linked to healthy metabolism and weight management. It supports your gut barrier, helps manage metabolic inflammation, and works with your body's natural weight regulation systems.", "supportingFindings": ["Insulin resistance / visceral adiposity phenotype (gut-metabolic axis support)", "Inflammatory phenotype (gut-immune axis)", "ApoB 117 mg/dL (atherogenic metabolic pattern)", "hs-CRP 3.3 mg/L (metabolic inflammation)"]}, {"dose": "1 chewable gel daily", "name": "NutraGems® CoQ10 300", "caution": "Chewable 300mg CoQ10 in emulsified form for enhanced absorption. Supports heart muscle function, energy production, and antioxidant protection. Essential for patients on statins.", "category": "cardiovascular", "priority": "medium", "rationale": "NutraGems CoQ10 300 provides high-potency ubiquinone for cardiovascular protection, cellular energy production, and antioxidant support. Essential for patients on statin therapy, which depletes CoQ10.", "indication": "ApoB 117 mg/dL (cardiovascular support); hs-CRP 3.3 mg/L", "phenotypes": ["Inflammatory Burden", "Oxidative Stress Burden"], "confidenceLevel": "moderate", "patientExplanation": "CoQ10 is a vital nutrient your body uses for energy production and heart health. This chewable supplement supports your cardiovascular system and helps maintain cellular energy, especially important as natural production declines with age.", "supportingFindings": ["ApoB 117 mg/dL (cardiovascular support)", "hs-CRP 3.3 mg/L"]}, {"dose": "1 capsule daily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Women's Probiotic", "caution": "5-in-1 multi-benefit probiotic with Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 for vaginal and urinary health. Increase to 2 daily for urogenital irritation.", "category": "probiotic", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete Women's provides 5-in-1 support for vaginal, urinary, digestive, and immune health with clinically studied Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 strains.", "indication": "Foundational women's probiotic support", "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This women-specific probiotic supports digestive health, vaginal and urinary tract balance, and immune function with clinically proven strains.", "supportingFindings": ["Foundational women's probiotic support"]}], "adjustedRisk": {"lpaValue": 20, "apoBValue": 117, "lpaStatus": "normal", "apoBStatus": "borderline", "riskCategory": "low", "baseASCVDRisk": 0.20300365442599252, "hasElevatedLpa": false, "hasElevatedApoB": false, "adjustedCategory": "low", "clinicalGuidance": "Low risk (<5%) without risk enhancers. Focus on lifestyle modifications; reassess in 4-6 years.", "hasBorderlineLpa": false, "hasBorderlineApoB": true}, "cacStatinRec": {"statinDiscussion": {"strength": "generally_recommended", "indicated": true, "rationale": "ApoB ≥90 mg/dL (117 mg/dL) with risk enhancers (elevated hs-CRP, elevated ApoB). Statin discussion recommended."}, "triglycerideMgmt": {"elevated": false, "severity": "normal", "recommendation": "Triglycerides within normal range."}, "cacRecommendation": {"priority": "none", "rationale": "CAC generally less informative under age 40. Consider if extreme family history with very high Lp(a).", "recommended": false}}, "recheckWindow": "3-6 months (routine follow-up)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall assessment\\nYour labs show many strengths but a few areas to improve. Your 10-year ASCVD risk is very low at 0.2% and 10-year total CVD risk is 0.3%, which is reassuring. However, hs-CRP is elevated at 3.3 mg/L (this is a marker of inflammation and is associated with increased cardiovascular risk). You also have borderline low total testosterone at 13.3 ng/dL and vitamin D is slightly insufficient at 37.2 ng/mL. Apolipoprotein B is borderline elevated at 117 mg/dL, which can reflect the number of atherogenic cholesterol particles even though your LDL is good.\\n\\nPositive findings (what’s working well)\\n- Hemoglobin 13.7 g/dL and hematocrit 41.1% — iron status looks healthy.\\n- Ferritin 52.1 ng/mL — iron stores are in the optimal range (>50).\\n- TSH 1.0 mIU/L — thyroid function is normal.\\n- Hemoglobin A1c 4.9% — excellent blood sugar control.\\n- LDL 90 mg/dL, HDL 61 mg/dL, triglycerides 61 mg/dL — favorable cholesterol profile.\\n- Lp(a) 20 mg/dL and eGFR 111 mL/min — good kidney function and low genetic risk marker.\\n\\nAreas to improve (specific values + actions)\\n- hs-CRP 3.3 mg/L (elevated): Adopt anti-inflammatory habits — aim for 150 minutes/week of moderate exercise (brisk walking, cycling), follow a Mediterranean-style diet (vegetables, whole grains, olive oil, fish, nuts), reduce processed foods and added sugars, prioritize 7–8 hours sleep, and manage stress (10–20 minutes daily meditation or brisk walking). Repeat hs-CRP in 3 months; if still >3 mg/L, discuss further evaluation with your provider.\\n- Apolipoprotein B 117 mg/dL (borderline): Increase soluble fiber (aim 25–30 g/day — oatmeal for breakfast, beans at lunch, vegetables at dinner), include fatty fish 2–3x weekly (salmon, mackerel, sardines), reduce saturated fat (choose lean meats, limit butter/cheese), and continue daily activity (30 minutes brisk walk).\\n- Total Testosterone 13.3 ng/dL (low): If you have symptoms (low libido, low energy), try sleep hygiene (7–8 hours), strength training 2–3x/week, and stress reduction; recheck testosterone in the morning and consider specialist referral if symptoms persist.\\n- Vitamin D 37.2 ng/mL (insufficient): Start vitamin D3 1,000–2,000 IU daily, get 10–20 minutes sun exposure several times a week, and recheck 25-OH vitamin D in 3 months. For bone health, ensure calcium intake ~1,000–1,200 mg/day and weight-bearing exercise.\\n\\nNext steps and timeline\\n- Start the lifestyle changes above now. Begin vitamin D supplement today and implement fiber/fish/sat-fat changes.\\n- Repeat hs-CRP, ApoB, and vitamin D in ~3 months.\\n- Reassess testosterone if you have related symptoms; time tests with provider to match your cycle and morning hours.\\n- Discuss any persistent inflammation or symptoms with your clinician for possible further testing or referrals.\\n\\nYou’re doing many things right — these targeted steps can lower inflammation and optimize hormones and heart health.", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 13.7, "status": "normal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "interpretation": "Hemoglobin within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "12-16 g/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 41.1, "status": "normal", "category": "Hematocrit", "interpretation": "Hematocrit within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "36-44%"}, {"unit": "fL", "value": 86.5, "status": "normal", "category": "MCV", "interpretation": "MCV 86.5 fL is within normal range (80–100 fL), indicating normal-sized red blood cells.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "80-100 fL"}, {"unit": "K/uL", "value": 301, "status": "normal", "category": "Platelets", "interpretation": "Platelet count within normal range.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "150-400 K/uL"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 38, "status": "normal", "category": "Estradiol", "interpretation": "Estradiol level recorded. Interpretation depends on menstrual phase.", "recommendation": "For accurate interpretation, document cycle day or menstrual phase.", "referenceRange": "20-500 pg/mL (varies by cycle phase)"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 0.25, "status": "normal", "category": "Progesterone", "interpretation": "Progesterone level 