ily", "name": "UltraFlora® Complete Women's Probiotic", "caution": "5-in-1 multi-benefit probiotic with Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 for vaginal and urinary health. Increase to 2 daily for urogenital irritation.", "category": "probiotic", "priority": "low", "rationale": "UltraFlora Complete Women's provides 5-in-1 support for vaginal, urinary, digestive, and immune health with clinically studied Lactobacillus GR-1 and RC-14 strains.", "indication": "Foundational women's probiotic support", "confidenceLevel": "supportive", "patientExplanation": "This women-specific probiotic supports digestive health, vaginal and urinary tract balance, and immune function with clinically proven strains.", "supportingFindings": ["Foundational women's probiotic support"]}], "cacStatinRec": {"statinDiscussion": {"strength": "generally_recommended", "indicated": true, "rationale": "Persistent non-HDL ≥160 mg/dL (184 mg/dL) indicates elevated atherogenic lipoprotein burden. Statin discussion recommended."}, "triglycerideMgmt": {"elevated": false, "severity": "normal", "recommendation": "Triglycerides within normal range."}, "cacRecommendation": {"priority": "consider", "rationale": "Lipid levels meet threshold for CAC consideration. CAC may be useful if risk level is uncertain or patient is hesitant about statin.", "recommended": false}}, "recheckWindow": "3-6 months (routine follow-up)", "patientSummary": "Here is a copy of your recent lab results, along with the recommendations.\\n\\nOverall assessment\\nYou have laboratory results consistent with menopause (FSH 41.6 mIU/mL) and a borderline heart risk profile (10-year total CVD risk 7.1%). Many values are reassuring (normal TSH 0.98 mIU/L, hemoglobin 14.2 g/dL, HDL 86 mg/dL). A few areas deserve follow-up and concrete lifestyle steps now: LDL cholesterol 159 mg/dL, vitamin B12 276 pg/mL (low‑normal), MCV 98.5 fL (high‑normal), AST 34 U/L (mildly high), hematocrit 45.1% (slightly high—possible dehydration), and estradiol 56 pg/mL with postmenopausal FSH.\\n\\nPositive findings (what’s good)\\n- TSH 0.98 mIU/L — normal thyroid function.\\n- Hemoglobin 14.2 g/dL and platelets 320 K/uL — good blood counts.\\n- HDL 86 mg/dL and triglycerides 123 mg/dL — protective lipid components.\\n- Hemoglobin A1c 5.4% — normal blood sugar control.\\n- eGFR 78 mL/min and creatinine 0.86 mg/dL — normal kidney function.\\n- FIB‑4 1.16 — low risk of advanced liver fibrosis.\\n\\nAreas to improve (specific values + actions)\\n- LDL cholesterol 159 mg/dL (above 130): start these dietary and activity steps now:\\n  - Add 25–30 g fiber daily: oatmeal for breakfast, beans at lunch, vegetables at dinner.\\n  - Include 2–3 servings fatty fish weekly (salmon, mackerel, sardines).\\n  - Reduce saturated fat: choose lean meats, limit butter and cheese.\\n  - Daily exercise: 30 minutes brisk walking (aim for 150 minutes/week total).\\n  - Because your 10‑year CVD risk is 7.1% (BORDERLINE), follow a Mediterranean-style diet, limit processed foods/added sugars, and discuss statin therapy with your provider; coronary calcium (CAC) scoring can help guide that choice.\\n- Vitamin B12 276 pg/mL and MCV 98.5 fL: increase B12 intake (eggs, dairy, fortified cereals, lean meat) and consider an oral B12 1,000 mcg daily for 8–12 weeks or discuss injection if you have symptoms (fatigue, numbness). Repeat CBC and B12 in 3 months.\\n- Hematocrit 45.1%: drink adequate fluids (aim for 1.5–2 L/day) and recheck labs when well‑hydrated.\\n- AST 34 U/L (mild): limit alcohol to <2 drinks/week, review medications/supplements that affect the liver, and maintain healthy weight. Recheck AST/ALT in 3 months.\\n- Estradiol 56 pg/mL with FSH 41.6 mIU/mL confirms menopause; if you develop hot flashes, sleep or mood changes, discuss hormone therapy options with your clinician.\\n\\nNext steps and timeline\\n- Start the diet/exercise steps today. Recheck fasting lipid panel, B12, CBC, and liver tests in ~3 months. Consider bone health screening (DEXA) and discuss menopause symptom management and whether statin therapy or CAC testing is right for you at your next visit. If new symptoms occur (numbness, worsening fatigue, heavy bleeding), contact your clinician sooner.\\n\\nYou’re doing well in many areas — these targeted changes can lower your heart and nutrient risks.", "interpretations": [{"unit": "g/dL", "value": 14.2, "status": "normal", "category": "Hemoglobin", "interpretation": "Hemoglobin within normal range for adult females.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "12-16 g/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 45.1, "status": "borderline", "category": "Hematocrit", "interpretation": "Slightly elevated hematocrit - may indicate dehydration.", "recommendation": "Encourage hydration. Repeat if persistent.", "referenceRange": "36-44%"}, {"unit": "fL", "value": 98.5, "status": "borderline", "category": "MCV", "interpretation": "MCV 98.5 fL is in the high-normal range. Early macrocytosis can precede overt B12 or folate deficiency.", "recommendation": "Ensure B12 and folate levels are within optimal range. Monitor CBC at next visit.", "referenceRange": "80-100 fL"}, {"unit": "K/uL", "value": 320, "status": "normal", "category": "Platelets", "interpretation": "Platelet count within normal range.", "recommendation": "Continue routine monitoring.", "referenceRange": "150-400 K/uL"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 56, "status": "borderline", "category": "Estradiol", "interpretation": "Estradiol elevated for postmenopausal status without HRT.", "recommendation": "Evaluate for exogenous estrogen source or ovarian pathology. Consider HRT if symptomatic.", "referenceRange": "<20 pg/mL (postmenopausal without HRT)"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 0.26, "status": "normal", "category": "Progesterone", "interpretation": "Progesterone appropriate for postmenopausal status.", "recommendation": "Expected finding.", "referenceRange": "<1 ng/mL (postmenopausal)"}, {"unit": "mIU/mL", "value": 41.6, "status": "normal", "category": "FSH", "interpretation": "Elevated FSH consistent with menopause.", "recommendation": "Expected finding for postmenopausal women.", "referenceRange": ">25 mIU/mL (postmenopausal)"}, {"unit": "ng/dL", "value": 29.2, "status": "normal", "category": "Testosterone (Total)", "interpretation": "Testosterone within normal female range.", "recommendation": "No intervention needed.", "referenceRange": "15-70 ng/dL"}, {"unit": "mIU/L", "value": 0.98, "status": "normal", "category": "TSH", "interpretation": "TSH within normal range - euthyroid.", "recommendation": "No thyroid intervention needed.", "referenceRange": "0.4-4.5 mIU/L"}, {"unit": "ng/mL", "value": 52.9, "status": "borderline", "category": "Vitamin D (25-OH)", "interpretation": "Vitamin D adequate but suboptimal (41-59 ng/mL).", "recommendation": "Metagenics D3 2000 Complex daily to reach optimal range ≥60 ng/mL.", "referenceRange": "≥60 ng/mL optimal"}, {"unit": "pg/mL", "value": 276, "status": "borderline", "category": "Vitamin B12", "interpretation": "Low-normal B12.", "recommendation": "Consider supplementation especially if symptomatic.", "referenceRange": "200-900 pg/mL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 5.4, "status": "normal", "category": "Hemoglobin A1c", "interpretation": "Normal glycemic control.", "recommendation": "Continue healthy lifestyle.", "referenceRange": "<5.7%"}, {"unit": "mg/dL", "value": 159, "status": "borderline", "category": "LDL Cholesterol", "interpretation": "Borderline high LDL.", "recommendation": "Lifestyle modifications. Consider statin if additional risk factors.", "referenceRange": "<100 mg/dL optimal"}, {"unit": "mg/dL", "value": 86, "status": "normal", "category": "HDL Cholesterol", "interpretation": "Good HDL level - protective.", "recommendation": "Maintain with regular exercise.", "referenceRange": "≥50 mg/dL (optimal ≥60)"}, {"unit": "mg/dL", "value": 123, "status": "normal", "category": "Triglycerides", "interpretation": "Normal triglycerides.", "recommendation": "Maintain healthy diet.", "referenceRange": "<150 mg/dL"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 7.08675620577023, "status": "borderline", "category": "10-Year Total CVD Risk (PREVENT)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "10-year cardiovascular disease risk: 7.1% (BORDERLINE RISK). Includes ASCVD and heart failure.", "recommendation": "Heart-healthy lifestyle: Mediterranean diet, regular exercise (150 min/week), maintain healthy weight, smoking cessation\\n\\nBORDERLINE RISK (5-7.5%): Consider coronary artery calcium (CAC) scoring\\n\\nStatin therapy based on shared decision-making if risk-enhancing factors present", "referenceRange": "Low <5%, Borderline 5-7.4%, Intermediate 7.5-19.9%, High ≥20%"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 4.334949694469105, "status": "borderline", "category": "10-Year ASCVD Risk (PREVENT)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "10-year ASCVD risk (heart attack, stroke): 4.3%", "recommendation": "Consider statin if risk-enhancing factors present. CAC scoring may help guide decision.", "referenceRange": "Heart attack & stroke risk"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 4.8712277364110195, "status": "normal", "category": "10-Year Heart Failure Risk (PREVENT)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "10-year heart failure risk: 4.9%", "recommendation": "Monitor for symptoms: shortness of breath, fatigue, leg swelling.", "referenceRange": "Heart failure risk"}, {"unit": "points", "value": 2, "status": "normal", "category": "Sleep Apnea Risk (STOP-BANG)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation": "LOW RISK for obstructive sleep apnea (2/8 points)", "recommendation": "Low probability of moderate-severe OSA. Continue routine monitoring. Consider sleep study if persistent symptoms of excessive daytime sleepiness, loud snoring, or cardiovascular risk factors.", "referenceRange": "Low 0-2, Intermediate 3-4, High 5-8"}, {"unit": "%", "value": 28.232419115579845, "status": "borderline", "category": "30-Year CVD Risk (PREVENT)", "recheckTiming": "Annual", "interpretation":